<title>USA: Sears March same-store sales up one percent.</title>
<headline>Sears March same-store sales up one percent.</headline>
<dateline>HOFFMAN ESTATES, Ill. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sears, Roebuck and Co said Thursday its same-store domestic sales for the five weeks ended April 5 rose one percent.</p>
<p>This followed a 6.8 percent increase in March same store sales a year ago.</p>
<p>Total domestic store revenues for the five weeks ending April 5 were $2.54 billion, 7.3 percent above revenues of $2.37 billion for the five weeks ending April 6, 1996, Sears said.</p>
